    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, a local merchant renamed the old Elliott’s Store to Grant’s Store, a name still remembered by residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.chathamstartribune.com/opinion/article_aec7a86a-cc2d-44c6-b669-6b7002a9c51b.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "George Lee Hardy, born in 1867, grew up near Pigg’s Mill on Pudding Creek, a tributary of the Banister River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.chathamstartribune.com/opinion/article_aec7a86a-cc2d-44c6-b669-6b7002a9c51b.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Banister Hardy, George’s grandfather, founded a family that settled throughout the Dry Fork area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.chathamstartribune.com/opinion/article_aec7a86a-cc2d-44c6-b669-6b7002a9c51b.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Grant’s Store is considered one of the most historically valuable buildings in Dry Fork, reflecting the town’s commercial past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.chathamstartribune.com/opinion/article_aec7a86a-cc2d-44c6-b669-6b7002a9c51b.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "On September 27, 2024, an EF2 tornado struck the Dry Fork area, injuring one person and destroying a mobile home.",
